					<h1 class="title" title="Bhopal – Tour to City of Lakes">Bhopal – Tour to City of Lakes</h1>
					<div class="entry-content">

<h3>Introduction</h3>
<p>Bhopal is the capital of <b>Madhya Pradesh, India</b>. It is the 11th century city <b>Bhojpal</b>, founded 
by Raja Bhoj, but the present city was established by an Afghan soldier, Dost Mohammed (1707-1740).It is a 
fascinating amalgam of scenic beauty, old historic city and modern urban planning. The two lakes of Bhopal 
still dominate the city, and are indeed its nucleus. If that is not enough, an era of Nawabi opulence with 
<b>historic monuments</b> in its full architectural grandeur awaits you in <b>Bhopal</b>.</p>

<h3>How to reach here:</h3>
<p>Bhopal is on one of the two main <b>Delhi to Mumbai railway lines</b> and also on the main line to the 
southern state capitals of <b>Chennai, Hyderabad, Bangalore</b> and <b>Thiruvananthpuram</b>. There are 
direct trains to <b>Amritsar</b> and <b>Jammu Tawi</b> and also to <b>major towns in Madhya Pradesh</b>. It 
has regular flights to <b>Mumbai, Indore, Delhi, Gwalior, Guwahati, Goa, Indore</b> and <b>Lucknow</b>. There 
are extensive bus services (private and state) to cities within the region and interstate.</p>

<h3>Places to visit:</h3>
<strong><u>Mosques and Palaces</u></strong>

<p><b>Taj-ul-Masajid</b> is the largest mosque in the country. The most impressive features of the mosque are its main hall with inter-arched roof, broad facade, spacious courtyard, and smooth marble flooring.</p>
<p><b>Jama Masajid</b> is located at the centre of chowk bazar; a busy business centre of Bhopal.</p>
<p><b>Moti Masajid</b> is architecturally akin to Jama Masajid in Delhi. </p>
<p><b>Shaukat Mahal</b> is an architectural marvel and a cynosure of all eyes.</p>
<p><b>Sadar Manzil</b> is the, Hall of public audience of the former rulers of Bhopal.</p>

<strong><u>Museums</u></strong>
<p><b>Bharat Bhawan</b> is a centre for the performing and visual arts.</p>

<p><b>Manav Sangrahalaya</b> (Museum of Man kind) is an open-air exhibition of tribal house types located on Shamla Hills. </p>

<p><b>Regional Science Centre</b> located on the picturesque Shyamala Hills. This centre houses about 300 science exhibits in ‘Invention’ and ‘Fun Science’ galleries. </p>

<p><b>Birla Mandir</b> is situated at the highest point of Bhopal, atop area Hills. From this place you can have an overview of the entire Bhopal city. </p>

<strong><u>Lakes and Parks</u></strong>
<p><b>Bhopal Lake</b> was built by late parmar king Bhoj one thousand years ago, known as Upper Lake. There are facilities for exciting trips by sail, paddle, and motor-boats. <b>Lower Lake</b> is about two hundred years old. </p>

<p><b>Gufa Mandir</b> and <b>Khatlapura Mandir</b> are famous temples which attract lot of devotees and visitors. </p>
<p><b>Van Vihar</b> is the center of attraction for local as well as foreign tourists which is located on a hill near to upper lake in natural surroundings. </p>



